        <param>
          <type>u32</type>
          <declname>ChromaOffset</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Initialize the ISP -&gt; DisplayPort live output bridge. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Brings up the clock wizard, DC live input path, VTC, frmbuf_rd, live-input GPIO and the DP transmitter. After this call the DP link trains on hotplug and the DC continuously displays whatever frame frmbuf_rd points at.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Width</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Active width in pixels (e.g. 1920). </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Height</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Active height in pixels (e.g. 1080). </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MemCfmt</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Memory color format of the DDR frames written by the ISP (must be XVIDC_CSF_MEM_RGB8; other formats are skipped). </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Stride</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Frame buffer stride in bytes (from the frmbuf_wr setup). </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ChromaOffset</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Byte offset from luma base to chroma plane (unused for RGB).</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS on success, otherwise an error code.</para></simplesect>
Initialize the ISP -&gt; DisplayPort live output bridge. </para>        </detaileddescription>
